From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:42:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple-g5p: ring a phase's doorbell unless its own stamp
 retired it

The publish-time doorbell of a render phase was skipped when the
engine's completion-event count had moved since the job was armed.
The count is taken when the job starts, before its TA is published, and
with two jobs in flight the previous job's 3D completes during this
job's TA: its completion event moved the count, the 3D of this job was
taken for already retired, and its doorbell was never rung. The
firmware then did not consume the 3D command until something else woke
its scheduler; when nothing did, the event stream stayed silent for a
second and the job and its context were lost ("3d-silent"). Scenes
with long fragment phases hit it: glmark2 terrain lost its context in
two of about eleven runs.

Apple's TA and 3D submit paths ring the doorbell after every ring entry
without any retirement check, and a doorbell for an entry the firmware
already consumed adds no work. Skip it only when the phase's own stamp
words show the phase retired; keep the event count as evidence.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/render-user-wake.h | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/render-user-wake.h b/drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/render-user-wake.h
index c8fd0aa..a4650d5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/render-user-wake.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/apple-g5p/render-user-wake.h
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
  * repaired, never a power arm), dma_wmb(), R0+0xb00 = 0x10 | engine.  At most one attempt
  * per phase.  Never after a timeout or fault (the terminal latch's sticky `failed`), never
  * with the boot failed or stopped, never unpowered, never with an r74f bell in flight,
- * never once the phase shows any sign of retirement, never on a ring that is not exactly
+ * never once the phase's own stamp shows it retired, never on a ring that is not exactly
  * this publish.  A consumer already at the target does not cancel (Apple never checks
  * it); it is recorded.  The natural TA completion (terminal kind COMPLETE, the epoch's
  * first note) is not a failure: the factor's sequence is the one licensed exception to the
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@ enum g5p_wk_did {
 	G5P_WK_SKIP_POWER, /* one of G5P_WK_PWR_REQUIRED is absent */
 	G5P_WK_SKIP_R74F, /* an r74f bell is published, open or firing */
 	G5P_WK_SKIP_RING, /* the ring is not exactly this publish */
-	G5P_WK_SKIP_RETIRED, /* a stamp == seq or a completion event since the publish */
+	G5P_WK_SKIP_RETIRED, /* a stamp == seq: this phase retired */
 	G5P_WK_SKIP_FENCE, /* R1+0x14 read back outside 7: no further register */
 	G5P_WK_SKIP_GPC, /* GPC not active: no 0xb00 */
 	G5P_WK_DIDS,
@@ -120,7 +120,11 @@ struct g5p_wk_in {
 	u32 start, target, prod,
 		cons; /* ring: producer before this publish, our target, now */
 	u32 stamp[2]; /* this engine's stamp words */
-	u32 type1; /* this engine's completion events decoded since the phase armed */
+	/* This engine's completion events decoded since the job armed: evidence only.  With two
+	 * jobs in flight the previous job's completion lands here too, so it cannot tell that
+	 * this phase retired; the stamps can.
+	 */
+	u32 type1;
 };
 
 /* The register access of the factor, in order.  The kernel binds them to writel/readl on the
@@ -221,7 +225,7 @@ static inline u32 g5p_wk_guard(const struct g5p_wk_in *in)
 	    in->cons > 255 || ((in->target - in->start) & 255) != 1 ||
 	    ((in->cons - in->start) & 255) > 1)
 		return G5P_WK_SKIP_RING;
-	if (in->stamp[0] == in->seq || in->stamp[1] == in->seq || in->type1)
+	if (in->stamp[0] == in->seq || in->stamp[1] == in->seq)
 		return G5P_WK_SKIP_RETIRED;
 	return 0;
 }
